%% Reactor devtools MCP loop. A running app with --devtools opens a
%% loopback HTTP listener and writes a lockfile at %TEMP%/reactor-devtools/
%% advertising endpoint + bearer token. The CLI reads the lockfile, POSTs
%% a JSON-RPC tools/call envelope, the in-app dispatcher hops the call
%% to the UI thread, the tool handler runs against the live tree (the
%% same tree the in-app DevtoolsMenu observes), and the result returns
%% as a JSON-RPC response. The in-app dev menu is local-only and shares
%% the same UseDevtools gate.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant CLI as mur devtools CLI
    participant LF as Lockfile<br/>(%TEMP%/reactor-devtools/<hash>.json)
    participant Server as DevtoolsMcpServer<br/>(HttpListener / stdio)
    participant Disp as McpDispatcher<br/>+ McpToolRegistry
    participant UI as UI thread<br/>(DispatcherQueue)
    participant Menu as In-app DevtoolsMenu<br/>(UseDevtools gate)

    CLI->>LF: read endpoint + bearer token
    CLI->>Server: POST /mcp · Authorization: Bearer …<br/>{"method":"tools/call","params":{...}}
    Server->>Disp: Dispatch(body)
    Disp->>UI: hop via DispatcherQueue.TryEnqueue
    UI->>UI: run tool handler against live tree
    UI-->>Disp: JSON result
    Disp-->>Server: JsonRpcResponse
    Server-->>CLI: HTTP 200 · JSON-RPC envelope

    Note over Menu,UI: Same UseDevtools() gate
    Menu->>UI: ToggleMenuItem · MenuItem click
    Menu->>UI: ReactorFeatureFlags · Observable<bool>
